# Agent Context, Memory & Docs Protocol

## Memory (memory-1)

Project memory lives in `memory/` as plain Markdown and is tracked in git, so it follows the branch.

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `memory/NOW.md` | What we are doing, what was just done, what is next, open questions. Overwritten every time. |
| `memory/MEMORY.md` | Index: one line per note, grouped by type. Read at session start. |
| `memory/notes/<slug>.md` | One dated fact per file: decision, preference, incident, gotcha or context. |
| `memory/LATER.md` | Open items that are not next; not read at session start. |
| `memory/archive/` | The pre-memory-1 `activeContext.md` / `progress.md` / `decisions.md`, kept as history. Do not update. |

### Session start
1. Read `memory/NOW.md`, then `memory/MEMORY.md`.
2. Check `NOW.md` against `git log` / `git status` since its date; work listed as next may already be done.
3. Open individual notes only when the task touches them. Code at HEAD wins for current behaviour; notes win for why
   and history; the newest current note wins between notes.

### When to write
- **`NOW.md`**: the plan changes, a blocker appears, work concludes, or the session ends with work done. Rewrite it from
  scratch (at most 50 lines); never append an "Earlier" trail.
- **A note**: a durable decision (with why and rejected options), a preference or correction from the user, an incident
  with its cause and fix, a non-obvious gotcha, or project context that is not in the repository.
- **`LATER.md`**: something a person would act on later that is not one of the next steps. `(User)` lines are for what
  the user owes; your own follow-ups go under `## Suggestions` and must name a real cost.
- **Supersede, do not rewrite**: when a decision changes, write a new note with `supersedes: <old-slug>`; set the old
  note to `status: superseded` and `superseded_by: <new-slug>`. Move its index line to History.
- After any memory change, run
  `python3 .agents/skills/memory-1/scripts/memory_check.py --memory memory` and fix every `FIX` line.

### Never write to memory
- Worktree cleanup / deletion — per-developer local hygiene, and recording it in tracked memory causes merge noise.
- Secrets, or anything the code, tests or docs already say.

## Docs (docs-1)

Docs live in `docs/` with docs-1 frontmatter. Start at [`docs/INDEX.md`](../../docs/INDEX.md).

- Read the index, then only the docs whose line answers the question.
- Before changing code, run `python3 .agents/skills/docs-1/scripts/docs_index.py covers <path>...` and update the
  docs that cover those files in the same change.
- New doc: copy the `docs-1` template, take the next ID from `docs_index.py next-id`, fill `summary` / `type` /
  `covers`, then run `docs_index.py write` and `docs_index.py check`.
- A doc replaced by another gets `status: superseded`, `superseded_by`, and moves to `docs/archive/`. Never delete a doc
  with history value.
- `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` and licence files stay where they are and are not indexed.

## Version control

`memory/` and `docs/` are tracked project state, not scratch. Commit them with the feature work or in a `memory:` /
`docs:` commit; do not leave the tree permanently dirty. Never delete note files or doc history to resolve a merge.
